### B4 – Final Engineering Decision

### B4.1 – Dynamic Memory

Dynamic memory allocation is suitable for donor lists because the number of donors can change. `realloc()` allows the list to grow when needed.

### B4.2 – File Storage

Text files are best for donor details because they are easy to read. Binary files are better for blood stock because they allow faster direct updates.

### B4.3 – Final Choice

I choose dynamic memory allocation, binary stock storage, and text donor storage because they provide good performance, flexibility, and easy maintenance.
